      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "وَ رُوِيَ عَنْ سُلَيْمَانَ بْنِ حَفْصٍ الْمَرْوَزِيِّ أَنَّهُ قَالَ:",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And it is narrated from Sulaymān ibn Ḥafṣ al-Marwazī that he said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "كَتَبَ إِلَيَّ أَبُو الْحَسَنِ الرِّضَا عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ «قُلْ فِي سَجْدَةِ الشُّكْرِ مِائَةَ مَرَّةٍ: شُكْرًا شُكْرًا وَ إِنْ شِئْتَ عَفْوًا عَفْوًا.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Abū al-Ḥasan al-Riḍā عليه السلام wrote to me: “Say in the prostration of gratitude one hundred times: ‘Shukran, shukran,’ and if you wish: ‘Afwan, afwan.’"
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith transmits an instruction from Imam al-Riḍā عليه السلام regarding what should be said in Sajdat al-Shukr. It teaches repeating words of gratitude, or alternatively asking pardon, as a devotional formula in the prostration of thankfulness.",
      "seo_question": "What should be recited in Sajdat al-Shukr according to Imam al-Riḍā عليه السلام?",
      "key_terms": {
        "سَجْدَةِ": "the prostration performed here as an act of devotion",
        "الشُّكْرِ": "gratitude or thankfulness shown to Allah",
        "مِائَةَ": "one hundred, indicating the recommended number of repetitions",
        "شُكْرًا": "an expression of thankfulness recited in the prostration",
        "عَفْوًا": "an expression seeking pardon or forbearance"
      }
    }
  },
